[' Due to the complexity of the task and the need for a comprehensive solution, I will outline the structure and key components of your `generate_records` function in C. This implementation assumes the use of Pthread for concurrency, Google's Protocol Buffers (protobuf) for efficient data representation, and a custom logging library that supports retries for transient failures.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <pthread.h>
#include <time.h>
#include <google/protobuf/message.h> // For logging protobuf message

// Define Record protobuf message
// (Replace with your actual implementation)
struct record {
  int64 offset;
  int64 key;
  int32 value;
};

// Logging interface for writing messages to external service
void log_message(const google::protobuf::Message* message);

// Function for initializing resources, including protobuf schema and thread-safe logging instance
void init();

// Thread-safe function for generating a record
void generate_record(int64 offset, int64 key, int32 value) {
  // Allocate memory for the record
  Record* record = (Record*) malloc(sizeof(Record));
  if (!record) {
    // Log error and free any allocated resources if a failure occurs
    log_error("Memory allocation failure");
    return;
  }

  // Initialize the record with given parameters
  record->offset = offset;
  record->key = key;
  record->value = value;

  // Create a protobuf message from the record and log it
  RecordMsg record_msg;
  record_msg.set_allocated_record(record);
  google::protobuf::Message* msg = record_msg.New();
  log_message(msg);
}

// Main function for generating records in a multi-threaded manner
void generate_records(int num_threads, int total_records) {
  init(); // Initialize resources

  pthread_t threads[num_threads];
  for (int i = 0; i < num_threads; ++i) {
    pthread_create(&threads[i], nullptr, generate_records_worker, &total_records);
  }

  for (int i = 0; i < num_threads; ++i) {
    pthread_join(threads[i], nullptr);
  }

  // Clean up resources when done
  cleanup();
}

// Worker function executed by each thread in the generate_records call
void* generate_records_worker(void* arg) {
  int64 total_records = *(int*)arg;
  int64 num_records_per_thread = total_records / num_threads;

  for (int i = 0; i < num_records_per_thread; ++i) {
    // Generate a record and log it
    generate_record(i * num_records_per_thread, i, i);
  }

  return nullptr;
}
```

This implementation provides a starting point for your `generate_records` function. You'll need to implement the missing pieces, such as the actual Record protobuf message, the logging functions, and the resource initialization, cleanup, and error handling functions. Make sure to optimize for performance, scalability, and robustness, and include tests to verify functionality under different scenarios.']

