Now, create a logging interface and an implementation:

```java
public interface Logger {
    void log(String message);
}

import ch.qos.logback.classic.Logger;
import ch.qos.logback.classic.spi.ILoggingEvent;
import ch.qos.logback.core.read.ListAppender;

public class SimpleLogger implements Logger {
    private final Logger logger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(SimpleLogger.class);

    public void log(String message) {
        ILoggingEvent event = new ILoggingEvent();
        event.setMessage(message);
        ListAppender<ILoggingEvent> appender = new ListAppender<>(logger, LayoutWrappingConverterToSerializable.createLayout());
        appender.start();
        appender.add(event);
        appender.stop();
    }
}
```

This simple logging implementation uses Logback for console and file output. You can extend this class to handle remote sinks like Google Cloud Pub/Sub or AWS CloudWatch, implement error handling, and add other features as needed."]

