2. Service Class:
```java
@Service
public class MostStateService {
    private final String cacheKey = "mostState";
    @Autowired
    private HazelcastInstance hazelcast;
    private Loader loader;

    // Constructor, autowired Feign client for checksum validation, external configuration service, and performance metrics

    public MoSTState load() {
        // Check if in cache
        MoSTState mostState = (MoSTState) hazelcast.getLocalCache(cacheKey).get(cacheKey);

        // If not in cache or expired
        if (mostState == null || System.currentTimeMillis() > mostState.getExpirationTime()) {
            synchronized (this) {
                // Load from file and validate checksum
                mostState = loader.loadFromFileAndValidateChecksum();

                // Cache the result
                if (mostState != null) {
                    hazelcast.getLocalCache(cacheKey).set(cacheKey, mostState);
                }
            }
        }
        return mostState;
    }
}
```

3. Loader Class:
```java
public class Loader {
    // File path, checksum validation Feign client, and external configuration service

    public MoSTState loadFromFileAndValidateChecksum() throws IOException {
        // Load from file
        ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(new FileInputStream("filePath"));
        MoSTState mostState = (MoSTState) ois.readObject();
        ois.close();

        // Validate checksum asynchronously and non-blocking
        CompletableFuture<Boolean> future = checksumValidationClient.validateChecksum(mostState);
        boolean valid = future.get();

        if (!valid) {
            return null;
        }

        // Update mostState with other data (e.g., external configuration service) and handle retries if needed

        return mostState;
    }
}
